<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phra Prang Sam Yot</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wat Phra Prang Sam Yot</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phra Prang Sam Yot is a temple in Lopburi, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, with three linked towers in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> style. Built around the late 12th or early 13th century, probably as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> shrine, it was later converted to Buddhist use. It is the symbol of Lopburi and known for the troops of monkeys that live around it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phra-prang-sam-yot.jpg" alt="Phra Prang Sam Yot" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mastertongapollo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%B8%9B%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%9B%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%84%E0%B9%8C%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%942.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
